# [DD-13b.W1.1 r46sem finding 3] `flags xmz` — ONLY `i` IS DEFINED. All
# three parsers must refuse this identically: leg A used to accept any
# run of letters and dump `flags=xmz`; leg B already refused it; leg C's
# `--dump` path (`parse_rxt`) used to accept it with no check at all,
# validating only in its separate oracle-check loop, which the C1
# differential never runs.
pattern a+
flags xmz
m "aaa" 0 3
